---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Contact from "../components/sections/Contact.astro";
import { profile } from "../content/profile";

const updated = "September 2026";
---

<SiteLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${profile.name}`}
  description="Privacy information for messages sent through Hassan Mushtaq's portfolio."
  initialHeaderTheme="light"
  skipHref="#privacy"
  skipLabel="Skip to privacy policy"
>
  <article class="policy" id="privacy">
    <header class="policy-head">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="mono policy-updated">( Last updated: {updated} )</p>
    </header>
    <div class="policy-body">
      <p>
        This policy explains how I, {profile.name}, a product designer and
        engineer based in {profile.location}, handle the personal information
        you share when you visit uxhassan.vercel.app (the “website”).
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>1. Who’s responsible</h2>
        <p>
          I run this website myself, so I’m the person responsible for your
          information. You can reach me at {profile.email}.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. What I collect</h2>
        <p>
          The only personal information I collect is what you choose to send
          me through the contact form or by email:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your name</li>
          <li>Your email address</li>
          <li>Your company, if you add it</li>
          <li>The details of your project or message</li>
        </ul>
        <p>There are no accounts or sign-ups on this website.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. How I use it</h2>
        <p>I use your information only to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Read and reply to your message</li>
          <li>
            Talk with you about the project, role or collaboration you raised
          </li>
          <li>Keep a record of our conversation while it’s ongoing</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          I never sell, rent or trade your information, and I won’t add you to
          a mailing list.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Legal basis (GDPR)</h2>
        <p>
          If you’re in the European Economic Area or the UK, I process your
          information based on:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your consent, which you give by ticking the box and sending the form</li>
          <li>My legitimate interest in replying to enquiries and discussing work with you</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Services involved</h2>
        <p>A few trusted services help run this website and deliver your message:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>FormSubmit (formsubmit.co) forwards the contact form to my inbox</li>
          <li>Google (Gmail) hosts my email</li>
          <li>
            Vercel hosts the website and, like any web host, may keep brief
            technical logs such as your IP address and browser type to keep the
            site secure
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Each handles data under its own privacy policy. If the form can’t
          send, it opens your own email app instead, and your message goes
          through your email provider.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. How long I keep it</h2>
        <p>
          I keep your messages only for as long as they’re useful for our
          conversation or any work that follows. You can ask me to delete them
          at any time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on where you live, you can:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Ask what information I hold about you</li>
          <li>Ask me to correct or delete it</li>
          <li>Withdraw your consent at any time</li>
          <li>Object to or restrict how I use it</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To do any of this, just email me.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This website doesn’t set any cookies and doesn’t use advertising or
          tracking tools.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Links to other websites</h2>
        <p>
          My case studies and profiles live on Behance, LinkedIn and Dribbble.
          When you follow those links, their own privacy policies apply.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If anything here changes, I’ll update this page and the date at the
          top.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy or your information? Get in touch:
        </p>
        <p class="policy-signature">
          {profile.name}
          <br />
          {profile.location}
          <br />
          <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
  <Contact />
  <script>
    import { initPrivacyPage } from "../scripts/privacy-page";
    initPrivacyPage();
  </script>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  /* One narrow column, as a document: the title in the accent serif, the
     body small and plain, with numbered sections at body size. */
  .policy {
    width: min(600px, calc(100% - 2 * var(--gutter)));
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 170px 0 160px;
  }
  .policy-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .policy-head h1 {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 3.4vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .policy-updated {
    flex: none;
    margin-top: 6px;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .policy-body {
    margin-top: 56px;
    font-size: var(--text-body-small);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .policy-body section {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .policy-body h2 {
    font: inherit;
  }
  .policy-body ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 16px;
  }
  .policy-body a {
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(23 24 25 / 35%);
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .policy {
      padding: 130px 0 110px;
    }
    .policy-head {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 12px;
    }
    .policy-updated {
      margin-top: 0;
      order: 2;
    }
    .policy-body {
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
  }
</style>
